The "official" PEG has this:

bridi-tail <- bridi-tail-1 (gihek stag? KE-clause free* bridi-tail
KEhE-clause? free* tail-terms)?
SPACE bridi-tail-sa <- bridi-tail-start (term / !bridi-tail-start (sa-word
/ SA-clause !bridi-tail-start ) )* SA-clause &bridi-tail

bridi-tail-start <- ME-clause / NUhA-clause / NU-clause / NA-clause
!KU-clause / NAhE-clause !BO-clause / selbri / tag bridi-tail-start /
KE-clause bridi-tail-start / bridi-tail

bridi-tail-1 <- bridi-tail-2 (gihek !(stag? BO-clause) !(stag? KE-clause)
free* bridi-tail-2 tail-terms)*

bridi-tail-2 <- bridi-tail-3 (gihek stag? BO-clause free* bridi-tail-2
tail-terms)?


Could you please provide examples where gihek in bridi-tail, bridi-tail-1
and bridi-tail-2 rules matches? I just thought that only one type of gihek
in bridi tails was possible but PEG tells me otherwise so I want to
distinguish them when I face them in a real text.

